      "tag_type": "HA (1x or 2x)",
      "tag_length_aa": null,
      "linker": null,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression confirmed by non-permeabilised immunostaining; channels reach the plasma membrane. Electrophysiological function of the tagged channel was not explicitly reported in the cited paper, but the construct was used as the primary surface-detection tool, implying trafficking is intact. PMC8654947 fitness screen confirmed surface-expression tolerance.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The ledger provides multiple independent lines pinning the junction to exactly Phe147|Lys148 in full-length, membrane-anchored ASIC1a (PMC7870742 \u00d7 4 quotes; PMC8654947 \u00d7 1 quote). Python confirms seq[146]='F' and seq[147]='K', matching the paper's Phe147/Lys148 nomenclature exactly. Position 147 is 85 aa from the TM1 C-boundary (residue 62) and 291 aa from TM2 (residue 438), placing it deep in the large extracellular domain. The junction is described as a 'disordered exposed site' in the crystal structure. Two independent tag modalities (HA and FLAG) and two species (rat, human) all tolerate the insertion, giving high confidence. HA epitope (YPYDVPDYA, 1 or 2 copies) inserted between Phe147 and Lys148 of full-length membrane-anchored hASIC1a and rASIC1a. Channels detected on the cell surface by antibody labelling under non-permeabilised conditions (live-cell surface staining). A FLAG tag was independently inserted at the same junction in a domain-insertion surface-expression fitness screen (PMC8654947). The 2\u00d7HA construct (hASIC1a-147 2HA 148) gave improved epitope exposure relative to a C-terminal GFP fusion, confirming extracellular accessibility. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 32996060,
          "citation": "PMID 32996060",
          "claim": "To selectively label the channels exposed on the cell surface, an HA epitope was genetically inserted into the extracellular loop of rat ASIC1a (rASIC1a) or hASIC1a between residues Phe 147 and Lys 148 (ASIC1a- 147 HA 148 , see Fig. 1 A, upper panel)."
        }
      ],
      "plddt": null,
      "conservation_rank": null,
      "median_conservation": null
    },
    {
      "site_id": "ASIC1-internal-298-lit",
      "gene_symbol": "ASIC1",
      "uniprot_acc": "P78348",
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "det_path": null,
      "site_kind": "internal",
      "insert_after_residue": 298,
      "residue_before": "D",
      "residue_after": "L",
      "residue_label": "D298",
      "topology_state": "O",
      "extracellular": true,
      "compartment": "extracellular",
      "tag_type": "HA / pHluorin",
      "tag_length_aa": null,
      "linker": null,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression confirmed by non-permeabilised immunostaining (HA construct) and by pHluorin fluorescence at the cell surface. The pHluorin insertion demonstrates that a full folded domain (~27 kDa) is tolerated, strongly implying the channel folds and traffics correctly. Electrophysiological function not explicitly reported for these tagged constructs in the cited paper.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The ledger pins the junction to exactly Asp298|Leu299 in full-length hASIC1a (PMC7870742, multiple quotes). Python confirms seq[297]='D' and seq[298]='L', matching the paper's Asp298/Leu299 nomenclature exactly. Position 298 is 236 aa from TM1 (residue 62) and 140 aa from TM2 (residue 438), deep in the extracellular domain. The tolerance of pHluorin (~27 kDa, far larger than any short epitope tag) at this exact junction is exceptionally strong evidence that a short ALFA-tag insert would be well tolerated. Ranked second only because the F147|K148 site has one additional independent paper (PMC8654947). HA epitope (YPYDVPDYA, 1 copy) inserted between Asp298 and Leu299 of full-length membrane-anchored hASIC1a; surface detection improved under non-permeabilised conditions relative to the original GFP-hASIC1a-147HA148 construct. The same junction was subsequently used to insert pHluorin (pH-sensitive GFP variant, ~27 kDa), a much larger domain, confirming robust structural tolerance at this site. Both constructs are described as 'centrally located in a disordered exposed site of the extracellular loop'. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 32996060,
          "citation": "PMID 32996060",
          "claim": "For the hASIC1a- 298 pHluorin 299 plasmid, the HA tag between Asp 298 and Leu 299 was replaced by the pH-sensitive GFP variant pHluorin."
        }
      ],
      "plddt": null,
